# Shell line editor: CLE, not readline.
#
# readline cannot move the cursor. It decodes exactly two escape sequences, 'A'
# and 'B' (up/down for history), and swallows the rest - so LEFT/RIGHT/HOME/END
# do nothing and fixing a typo means retyping the line. CLE decodes the full
# VT100 set (left, right, home, end, delete) and has its own history.
#
# What CLE lacks upstream is TAB completion; patches/nuttx-apps/0001 adds it,
# reusing the command list NSH already exposes to readline, so TAB completes
# NSH's own ls/ps/cat as well as the apps.
#
# CLE redraws the whole line itself on every keypress, so the DRIVER must not
# also echo or every character would appear twice. apps/serial and apps/init
# both clear ECHO before handing a port to a shell.
